%% Failed upgrade and rollback — Packaging & Distributing Your App.
%% Step 2 of the SA demo: the upgrade ships probes pointing at a path the service does not serve.
%% The new pod never becomes ready, so Helm never promotes the revision, the pods from revision 1
%% keep answering throughout, and one command returns the release to them. Authored 2026-09-12 for
%% the same reason as the sibling 05-chart-to-release.mmd: this module's other diagrams are
%% whole-module recaps, and a step is read as a picture before it is read as words.
%% ---
%% The two paths out of the upgrade ARE the point — the failing one and the one still serving — so
%% they converge on the rollback rather than leaving a dead end. Flat LR, no subgraph: a subgraph
%% that declares `direction` and has an edge crossing its boundary has that `direction` silently
%% discarded (02-olm-anatomy.mmd's header carries the measurements).
%% ---
%% NEVER put an angle-bracket placeholder in a .mmd file. Antora emits mermaid source into the page
%% UNESCAPED, so a word wrapped in angle brackets becomes a REAL DOM element that swallows the rest
%% of the graph; the line-break tag is the only markup safe inside a label. Write placeholders in
%% CAPS. Second trap, same symptom: a BARE "%%" line with no text after it defeats mermaid's comment
%% stripper and the diagram dies the same silent way — always put text after %%, as "%% ---" does.
graph LR
  up["helm upgrade --wait<br/>probes moved to /healthz"] --> new["new pod 0/1<br/>readiness 404s"]
  up --> old["revision 1 pods 1/1<br/>still answering /health"]
  new --> fail["UPGRADE FAILED<br/>revision never promoted"]
  fail --> rb["helm rollback<br/>one command, no outage"]
  old --> rb
  classDef bad fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  classDef good fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef act fill:#e8eaf6,stroke:#3949ab,color:#1a237e;
  class new,fail bad; class old good; class up,rb act;
